From: Kernel patch series <noreply@example.com>
Subject: [PATCH 5/5] arm64: dts: mediatek: mt8188: fix Panfrost IRQ names

Panfrost requests the GPU interrupts by the lowercase names "job",
"mmu" and "gpu". Use those names in the MT8188 GPU node so that
Panfrost can retrieve its IRQ resources during probe.

This fixes the probe failure:
  panfrost 13000000.gpu: error -ENXIO: IRQ gpu not found

The interrupt specifiers and their order are unchanged.

---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt8188.dtsi | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt8188.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt8188.dtsi
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt8188.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt8188.dtsi
@@ -2237,1 +2237,1 @@
-			interrupt-names = "JOB", "MMU", "GPU";
+			interrupt-names = "job", "mmu", "gpu";
